["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Quail do not migrate. The same covey lives in the same draw all year, but its size, its calls and its habits change by the month. Know the month, know the bird.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel for California quail in BC. January and February: big winter coveys. March: coveys break up. April: pairs. May: nests. June: peak hatch. July: broods. August: families join together. September: coveys form. October and November: the Region 8 season, 1 October to 30 November, 99 percent. December: winter coveys. Biology 65 to 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The quail year</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 68.0 A96 96 0 0 1 248.0 80.9 L225.0 120.7 A50 50 0 0 0 200.0 114.0 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"218.89379029248403\" y=\"98.48741468089801\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text>\n<text x=\"227.95245687107223\" y=\"62.748159108202486\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M248.0 80.9 A96 96 0 0 1 283.1 116.0 L243.3 139.0 A50 50 0 0 0 225.0 120.7 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"251.618795026618\" y=\"117.38120497338204\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text>\n<text x=\"276.3675323681471\" y=\"91.21825406947978\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M283.1 116.0 A96 96 0 0 1 296.0 164.0 L250.0 164.0 A50 50 0 0 0 243.3 139.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"270.51258531910196\" y=\"150.10620970751597\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n<text x=\"304.31998923921935\" y=\"140.52990503872272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">break up</text>\n<path d=\"M296.0 164.0 A96 96 0 0 1 283.1 212.0 L243.3 189.0 A50 50 0 0 0 250.0 164.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"270.51258531910196\" y=\"187.89379029248403\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n<text x=\"304.31998923921935\" y=\"197.47009496127728\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">pairs</text>\n<path d=\"M283.1 212.0 A96 96 0 0 1 248.0 247.1 L225.0 207.3 A50 50 0 0 0 243.3 189.0 Z\" fill=\"#b9a88a\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"251.618795026618\" y=\"220.61879502661796\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text>\n<text x=\"276.3675323681471\" y=\"246.78174593052023\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">nests</text>\n<path d=\"M248.0 247.1 A96 96 0 0 1 200.0 260.0 L200.0 214.0 A50 50 0 0 0 225.0 207.3 Z\" fill=\"#b9a88a\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"218.89379029248403\" y=\"239.512585319102\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n<text x=\"227.95245687107223\" y=\"275.25184089179754\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">hatch</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 260.0 A96 96 0 0 1 152.0 247.1 L175.0 207.3 A50 50 0 0 0 200.0 214.0 Z\" fill=\"#b9a88a\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181.10620970751597\" y=\"239.512585319102\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text>\n<text x=\"172.04754312892774\" y=\"275.25184089179754\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">broods</text>\n<path d=\"M152.0 247.1 A96 96 0 0 1 116.9 212.0 L156.7 189.0 A50 50 0 0 0 175.0 207.3 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"148.38120497338204\" y=\"220.618795026618\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n<text x=\"123.63246763185288\" y=\"246.78174593052023\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">families</text>\n<path d=\"M116.9 212.0 A96 96 0 0 1 104.0 164.0 L150.0 164.0 A50 50 0 0 0 156.7 189.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"129.48741468089804\" y=\"187.89379029248403\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"95.68001076078063\" y=\"197.4700949612773\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M104.0 164.0 A96 96 0 0 1 116.9 116.0 L156.7 139.0 A50 50 0 0 0 150.0 164.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"129.487414680898\" y=\"150.10620970751597\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n<text x=\"95.68001076078062\" y=\"140.52990503872272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">SEASON</text>\n<path d=\"M116.9 116.0 A96 96 0 0 1 152.0 80.9 L175.0 120.7 A50 50 0 0 0 156.7 139.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"148.381204973382\" y=\"117.38120497338204\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n<text x=\"123.63246763185285\" y=\"91.21825406947978\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">SEASON</text>\n<path d=\"M152.0 80.9 A96 96 0 0 1 200.0 68.0 L200.0 114.0 A50 50 0 0 0 175.0 120.7 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181.106209707516\" y=\"98.48741468089801\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n<text x=\"172.04754312892777\" y=\"62.748159108202486\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">coveys</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 1 to</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov 30</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Coveys in fall and winter, pairs in spring, broods in summer (70 to 80%).</li><li>Season: 1 October to 30 November in Region 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how sure is this chapter</summary><ul><li>Most timing data come from California studies <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. BC birds live farther north and dates may run later: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> against BC records.</li><li>The BC atlas and the app's migration data agree: no migration, the same low country all year (60 to 85%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of covey size. BC usual: under 30 birds, BC Breeding Bird Atlas, 85 percent. California average: 20 to 25, 70 percent. Washington: a dozen to several dozen, 75 percent. BC big coveys: 100 or more at times, 85 percent. Tip: coveys merge in hard winters.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How many birds in a covey?</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">BC, usual</text>\n<rect x=\"132.3\" y=\"50\" width=\"66.69999999999999\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"207.0\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">under 30 (85%)</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">California avg</text>\n<rect x=\"176.0\" y=\"96\" width=\"11.5\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"195.5\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">20 to 25 (70%)</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Washington</text>\n<rect x=\"157.6\" y=\"142\" width=\"82.79999999999998\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"248.39999999999998\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">a dozen to several dozen (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">BC, big ones</text>\n<rect x=\"360.0\" y=\"188\" width=\"8\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#a33b2a\"/>\n<text x=\"354.0\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">100 or more (85%)</text>\n<line x1=\"130\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"384\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text>\n<line x1=\"187.5\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"187.5\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"187.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25</text>\n<line x1=\"245.0\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"245.0\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"245.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50</text>\n<line x1=\"302.5\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"302.5\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"302.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75</text>\n<line x1=\"360.0\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"360.0\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"360.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100</text>\n<text x=\"256\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">birds per covey</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Coveys merge in hard winters (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Big coveys near farms, orchards and thick brush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Hard winters are the main killer <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: winter in full</summary><ul><li>Winter coveys, sometimes very large, near farms, orchards and suburbs with thick brush; same small range all winter (75%, app migration data).</li><li>In winter they form even bigger coveys, sometimes hundreds of birds (60%, Okanagan naturalist in iNFOnews).</li><li>California winter home range of four coveys averaged 10.5 ha (26 acres), from 6.9 to 18 ha <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Winter movements cover about twice the area used in summer <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Snow: Tip, 60%, from the quick lesson: snow after a cold night pushes coveys to sunny slopes and bare ground, closer to houses.</li><li>No season now. Scout only: drive back roads, listen, note coveys in the Journal (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gantt chart from California habitat records, 80 percent. Pairing March to early May. Nesting April to August, peak May and June. Broods from late May into September. About 14 eggs; the female incubates 22 to 23 days. Chicks run at once and fly short hops at about 10 days, 75 percent. BC dates may run later: VERIFY.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring and summer (California data)</text>\n<line x1=\"110\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"130\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n<line x1=\"150\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n<line x1=\"190\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text>\n<line x1=\"230\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n<line x1=\"270\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"290\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text>\n<line x1=\"310\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n<line x1=\"350\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Pairing</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"72\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Nesting</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"108\" width=\"200\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Peak</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"144\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Broods</text><rect x=\"210.0\" y=\"180\" width=\"176.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"222\" width=\"380\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">About 14 eggs, female sits 22 to 23 days (80%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chicks run at once, fly short hops at 10 days (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BC dates may run later: VERIFY</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Coveys break up in March. Pairing takes about 2 months <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Unpaired cocks give the single \"cow\" call from a high perch <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: spring in full</summary><ul><li>\"Approximately 2 months elapse between covey breakup in March and complete segregation of birds into pair bonds.\" (70%, Edgewood notes)</li><li>Pairs form from March to early May (80%, California habitat records).</li><li>Spring dispersal: a covey may spread up to 8 km (5 mi) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. App data: some birds disperse up to 8 km in April <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Males fight with the \"squill\" call while they sort out rank <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Courtship: the male droops his wings, spreads his tail, bobs his head and may rush at the female; courtship feeding by both sexes (70 to 75%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gantt chart from California habitat records, 80 percent. Pairing March to early May. Nesting April to August, peak May and June. Broods from late May into September. About 14 eggs; the female incubates 22 to 23 days. Chicks run at once and fly short hops at about 10 days, 75 percent. BC dates may run later: VERIFY.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring and summer (California data)</text>\n<line x1=\"110\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"130\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n<line x1=\"150\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n<line x1=\"190\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text>\n<line x1=\"230\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n<line x1=\"270\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"290\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text>\n<line x1=\"310\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n<line x1=\"350\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Pairing</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"72\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Nesting</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"108\" width=\"200\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Peak</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"144\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Broods</text><rect x=\"210.0\" y=\"180\" width=\"176.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"222\" width=\"380\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">About 14 eggs, female sits 22 to 23 days (80%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chicks run at once, fly short hops at 10 days (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BC dates may run later: VERIFY</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>About 14 eggs. The hen sits 22 to 23 days <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Chicks run at once and fly short hops at about 10 days <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: nesting in full</summary><ul><li>Nests April to August, peak May and June; most hatch in June (80%, California habitat records).</li><li>Clutch averages 14 (range 6 to 16, California records) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Audubon: 1 to 21, usually 13 to 14 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Two hens sometimes lay in one nest <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Laying: about 3 eggs every 4 days; incubation starts when the clutch is complete (70%, Edgewood notes).</li><li>Nest: a shallow scrape lined with grass and leaves, under a shrub, brush pile or log <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The male stands sentinel while the female incubates <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Young leave the nest within a day, follow the parents and feed themselves <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. The hen broods them at night for the first two weeks; they cannot hold their own heat yet <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>One brood a year, two in good years <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. In BC, one or possibly two clutches is more likely (65%, BC Outdoors).</li><li>Rain drives the hatch: high numbers follow wet winters with good green growth <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-female.jpg\" alt=\"A hen with a chick. By late summer, broods join into coveys.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A hen with a chick. By late summer, broods join into coveys. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan Vernon, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Callipepla_californica_-California,_USA_-female_and_chick-_8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Family groups join into coveys (60 to 70%).</li><li>Coveys of 20 or more by September <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: late summer in full</summary><ul><li>August: family groups join into coveys (60%, app migration data).</li><li>September: coveys of 20 or more in brushy draws and farm edges <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Broods use only a few acres in the first 2 weeks and 4 to 8 ha by one month (80%, California habitat records).</li><li>Moult: young birds replace most feathers through late summer but keep buff tipped coverts into fall (70%, 1963 Condor aging study, search preview). Exact moult months for BC birds: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>Watch broods in August from the road to guess the fall crop (Tip). Count chicks per hen and write it down.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Comparison of October and November for quail hunting, opinion. Leaves: many still on in October, mostly down in November. Coveys: formed in October, may merge in November. Cover: thick and hard to see into in October, thinner and easier in November. Weather: warm dry days in October, cold and first snow in November. Pressure: fresh birds in October, wiser birds in November. Region 8 season covers both months, 1 October to 30 November, 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">October vs November (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"38\" width=\"138\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">October</text>\n<rect x=\"252\" y=\"38\" width=\"138\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"321\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">November</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Leaves</text>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"72\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">many still on</text>\n<rect x=\"252\" y=\"72\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"321\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">mostly down</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Coveys</text>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"110\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">formed</text>\n<rect x=\"252\" y=\"110\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"321\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">formed, may merge</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Cover</text>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"148\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thick, hard to see</text>\n<rect x=\"252\" y=\"148\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"321\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thinner, easier</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Weather</text>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"186\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">warm days, dry</text>\n<rect x=\"252\" y=\"186\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"321\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cold, first snow</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Pressure</text>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"224\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fresh birds</text>\n<rect x=\"252\" y=\"224\" width=\"138\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"321\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">birds wiser</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Season both months: 1 Oct to 30 Nov (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Region 8 quail: 1 October to 30 November, 10 a day, 30 in possession <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Late October to mid November: leaves down, coveys formed (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: October and November in full</summary><ul><li>Rule Book, Region 8, page 68: \"QUAIL\", MUs (Management Units) 8-1 to 8-15 and 8-21 to 8-26, \"Oct 1 - Nov 30\", \"10 (30)\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. See the <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8 Rule Book</a>.</li><li>October: fall coveys in brushy draws, orchard and vineyard edges, riparian thickets (70%, app migration data).</li><li>November: coveys on winter range: brush, farm edges, riparian thickets <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>\"Best window: late October to mid November. Leaves are down, coveys are formed, and the season runs to 30 November.\" (Tip, from the <a href=\"#/s/local-okanagan\">Okanagan trip plan</a>)</li><li>Early October: thick leaves, warm days, fresh birds that hold. Late November: thin cover, cold, birds wiser after flushes (Tip).</li><li>Orchards and vineyards: harvest crews may be working in October. Ask where people are today (Tip, from the quick lesson).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel for California quail in BC. January and February: big winter coveys. March: coveys break up. April: pairs. May: nests. June: peak hatch. July: broods. August: families join together. September: coveys form. October and November: the Region 8 season, 1 October to 30 November, 99 percent. December: winter coveys. Biology 65 to 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The quail year</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 68.0 A96 96 0 0 1 248.0 80.9 L225.0 120.7 A50 50 0 0 0 200.0 114.0 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"218.89379029248403\" y=\"98.48741468089801\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text>\n<text x=\"227.95245687107223\" y=\"62.748159108202486\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M248.0 80.9 A96 96 0 0 1 283.1 116.0 L243.3 139.0 A50 50 0 0 0 225.0 120.7 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"251.618795026618\" y=\"117.38120497338204\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text>\n<text x=\"276.3675323681471\" y=\"91.21825406947978\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M283.1 116.0 A96 96 0 0 1 296.0 164.0 L250.0 164.0 A50 50 0 0 0 243.3 139.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"270.51258531910196\" y=\"150.10620970751597\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n<text x=\"304.31998923921935\" y=\"140.52990503872272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">break up</text>\n<path d=\"M296.0 164.0 A96 96 0 0 1 283.1 212.0 L243.3 189.0 A50 50 0 0 0 250.0 164.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"270.51258531910196\" y=\"187.89379029248403\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n<text x=\"304.31998923921935\" y=\"197.47009496127728\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">pairs</text>\n<path d=\"M283.1 212.0 A96 96 0 0 1 248.0 247.1 L225.0 207.3 A50 50 0 0 0 243.3 189.0 Z\" fill=\"#b9a88a\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"251.618795026618\" y=\"220.61879502661796\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text>\n<text x=\"276.3675323681471\" y=\"246.78174593052023\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">nests</text>\n<path d=\"M248.0 247.1 A96 96 0 0 1 200.0 260.0 L200.0 214.0 A50 50 0 0 0 225.0 207.3 Z\" fill=\"#b9a88a\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"218.89379029248403\" y=\"239.512585319102\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n<text x=\"227.95245687107223\" y=\"275.25184089179754\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">hatch</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 260.0 A96 96 0 0 1 152.0 247.1 L175.0 207.3 A50 50 0 0 0 200.0 214.0 Z\" fill=\"#b9a88a\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181.10620970751597\" y=\"239.512585319102\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text>\n<text x=\"172.04754312892774\" y=\"275.25184089179754\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">broods</text>\n<path d=\"M152.0 247.1 A96 96 0 0 1 116.9 212.0 L156.7 189.0 A50 50 0 0 0 175.0 207.3 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"148.38120497338204\" y=\"220.618795026618\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n<text x=\"123.63246763185288\" y=\"246.78174593052023\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">families</text>\n<path d=\"M116.9 212.0 A96 96 0 0 1 104.0 164.0 L150.0 164.0 A50 50 0 0 0 156.7 189.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"129.48741468089804\" y=\"187.89379029248403\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"95.68001076078063\" y=\"197.4700949612773\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M104.0 164.0 A96 96 0 0 1 116.9 116.0 L156.7 139.0 A50 50 0 0 0 150.0 164.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"129.487414680898\" y=\"150.10620970751597\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n<text x=\"95.68001076078062\" y=\"140.52990503872272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">SEASON</text>\n<path d=\"M116.9 116.0 A96 96 0 0 1 152.0 80.9 L175.0 120.7 A50 50 0 0 0 156.7 139.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"148.381204973382\" y=\"117.38120497338204\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n<text x=\"123.63246763185285\" y=\"91.21825406947978\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">SEASON</text>\n<path d=\"M152.0 80.9 A96 96 0 0 1 200.0 68.0 L200.0 114.0 A50 50 0 0 0 175.0 120.7 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181.106209707516\" y=\"98.48741468089801\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n<text x=\"172.04754312892777\" y=\"62.748159108202486\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">coveys</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 1 to</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov 30</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Season closed after 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Coveys settle on winter range near cover and food <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: December in full</summary><ul><li>The Region 8 quail season ends 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>December: winter coveys in thick cover near feed (75%, app migration data).</li><li>Use December to clean the Journal: where each covey was, how many birds, what cover (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Chukar (FEIS 80%)</th><th>Gray partridge (Audubon 75%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Feb to Apr</td><td>Pairs form</td><td>Coveys break into pairs</td></tr><tr><td>Apr to Jun</td><td>Eggs, about 15, 24 days</td><td>Eggs 12 to 18, about 25 days</td></tr><tr><td>Summer</td><td>Broods near water</td><td>Chicks eat insects</td></tr><tr><td>Fall</td><td>Coveys of about 20</td><td>Young stay with parents</td></tr><tr><td>Winter</td><td>Move down in deep snow</td><td>Burrow in snow for seeds</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Both: 1 October to 30 November in Regions 3 and 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: chukar and Hun year in full</summary><ul><li>Chukar pair from February to March or April. Egg laying averages about 20 April in Washington. Clutch 10 to 20, average 15; incubation typically 24 days; flights by about 2 weeks (80%, FEIS).</li><li>Chukar coveys form from one or more broods; males often rejoin the brood in early fall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Coveys about 20, sometimes 40 or more <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Chukar move from higher ground to lower terrain in heavy snow, and onto south facing slopes in bad weather <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Drought cuts chukar clutch size, and in extreme drought there may be no breeding <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Gray partridge: 12 to 18 eggs, incubation 21 to 26 days, usually 25; young fly short hops under 2 weeks and stay with the parents through the first winter (75%, Audubon).</li><li>Rules: chukar \"5 (15)\", gray partridge \"3 (9)\", both 1 October to 30 November in Regions 3 and 8 (99%, Rule Book).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gantt chart from California habitat records, 80 percent. Pairing March to early May. Nesting April to August, peak May and June. Broods from late May into September. About 14 eggs; the female incubates 22 to 23 days. Chicks run at once and fly short hops at about 10 days, 75 percent. BC dates may run later: VERIFY.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring and summer (California data)</text>\n<line x1=\"110\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"130\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n<line x1=\"150\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n<line x1=\"190\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text>\n<line x1=\"230\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n<line x1=\"270\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"290\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text>\n<line x1=\"310\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n<line x1=\"350\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Pairing</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"72\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Nesting</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"108\" width=\"200\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Peak</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"144\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Broods</text><rect x=\"210.0\" y=\"180\" width=\"176.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"222\" width=\"380\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">About 14 eggs, female sits 22 to 23 days (80%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chicks run at once, fly short hops at 10 days (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BC dates may run later: VERIFY</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"March they part, May they lay, June they hatch, fall they stay.\" (Tip, 70 to 80% for the months)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"14, 23, 10\": about 14 eggs, 23 days on the nest, chicks fly at 10 days (75 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Season hook:</strong> \"October first to November's end: ten a day, thirty to tend.\" (99% for the rule)</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"Wet spring, full covey.\" California data back it: rain and green growth drive the hatch <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>California wildlife habitat records, Edgewood notes, Audubon, FEIS, the app migration data, the Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://ncrcd.specialdistrict.org/files/b900df31f/California-Quail-info.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California Wildlife Habitat Relationships: California quail (Ahlborn, California Department of Fish and Game)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: pairing, nesting, clutch, home range, dispersal, rainfall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://friendsofedgewood.org/?p=5231\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Friends of Edgewood: California quail (Franks 2002, from Calkins et al. 1999)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/california-quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon field guide: California quail</a> and <a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/gray-partridge\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/database/feis/animals/bird/alch/all.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">US Forest Service FEIS: chukar (Sullivan 1994)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>App migration data (data/migration.json, quail entry, checked 2026-10-03) (60 to 75%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bcoutdoorsmagazine.com/?p=9278\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Outdoors: California quail (Harris 2021)</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. <a href=\"https: